## 6. Verification (what a build must satisfy)

| id | claim | test |
|---|---|---|
| IC-C1 | Intelligence-as-peer | an Intelligence is declared with a `channel` interface, `config`, `calibration`, `transactional` role; a bus peer messages it via `intelligence/<id>/in` and reads its reply on `.../out`, ignorant a mind is behind them |
| IC-C2 | duplex over channels | an inbound bus message on `.../in` arrives in-context as a `<channel>` event; a `reply`-tool call publishes to `.../out` — round-trip proven against a mock bus + mock MCP transport |
| IC-C3 | mine vs. bridge | the composeio-native channel backend runs with NO Haven dependency; `haven-dispatch` is reachable as an optional bridge backend only |
| IC-C4 | self-instrumentation | `self/context_level` reads from stdin `used_percentage` when present (authoritative) and falls back to the JSONL estimate; `self/registered` flips true iff a dusk-gift surface was read this session |
| IC-C5 | permission relay | a tool-approval `permission_request` publishes `.../permission/request`; a verdict on `.../permission/verdict` allows/denies the call; the local dialog stays live and first-answer wins |
| IC-C6 | self-directed `/compact` | the instance, at its chosen threshold, emits an authored direction on `.../out`; the launcher types `/compact <direction>` into its stdin; the launcher originates no direction of its own |
| IC-C7 | composable canvas | emitting a mermaid diagram on `thread/diagram` renders it in the widget with no model round-trip; the avatar renders an emitted `self/avatar/expression` |
| IC-C8 | define-once flavors | the work and theatrical widgets share one instance/channel/lifecycle/meta-object, differing only in scene |
| IC-C9 | graceful absence | with the channel absent, the Intelligence peer's namespaces go `health=down` and the rest of the bus is unaffected ([plt.cio:SPEC:DP-CIO-11]) |
| IC-C10 | question relay | a structured AUQ question publishes `.../question/request`; the widget renders N option cards; a verdict on `.../question/verdict` returns as the Intelligence's AUQ answer — proven without depending on channel-native AUQ support |
| IC-C11 | transcript streams, safety-by-construction | the tailer republishes `thread/narration`/`self/activity`/`self/subagents` from the JSONL transcript with thinking blocks dropped and `tool_result` content never republished; a narration payload shaped like a command is NOT actuated, because it never reaches `intelligence/<id>/out` |
| IC-C12 | avatar arbitration | with both publishers live, an explicit `self/avatar/expression` from the Intelligence always overrides the monitor's inferred one; with only the inferred publisher active, the avatar is never blank |
| IC-C13 | harness monitor | the statusline-sourced state file drives threshold crossings at 65/80/90 (fire-once, re-arm on drop), a heartbeat fires once per idle stretch, and `{"cmd":"context"}` returns the current reading — delivered as non-interrupting `<channel from="harness">` events on `intelligence/<id>/in` |
| IC-C14 | tailer durability, de-forked | a JSONL line appended across multiple flushes (a large `Agent` dispatch/completion) is delivered WHOLE by the shared partial-line-safe reader, never dropped as a fragment; `transcript_publisher` and `deliverable_monitor` both reuse that ONE reader — a split dispatch+completion still yields `self/subagents` dispatched-then-done, and a split `Write` still yields its deliverable path (`intelligence/publisher/test_tail_follow.py`) |
| IC-C15 | single-instance identity | two channel bridges launched for the SAME `<id>` resolve to exactly one live owner: the newer (later start-time) bridge KEEPS the identity and the older one is DISPLACED — it yields and exits — on hearing the newer bridge's heartbeat; a bridge is never displaced by its own beat nor by an OLDER peer (no reconnect-war), so a `/exit`+resume or a duplicate concurrent session cannot leave `.../in` fanning out or `.../channel/alive` masking link health (`node intelligence/channel/channel.mjs --selftest`, path f) |
| IC-C16 | self-reaping on client disconnect | the bridge exits(0) when its MCP client goes away — stdin EOF (`end`/`close`) or stdout EPIPE — even though the SDK stdio transport does NOT fire `onclose` on EOF; an orphaned bridge reaps ITSELF and is never left holding the bus identity (`--selftest` path h: a subprocess whose stdin is closed exits on its own; without the reaper it would hang) |
| IC-C17 | delivery-liveness | injects unacked past a threshold — no client→server call has proven the session is surfacing our notifications — flip the heartbeat to `delivery:"degraded"` (carrying the unacked count) so the console link dot reads RED not false-green; any client→server ack (a `reply`) clears it. The break (a client-side listener lost after churn) is thus DETECTED; recovery is a client-side `/mcp reconnect composeio-channel` (`--selftest` path g) |

